193
00:18:06,110 --> 00:18:09,030
[Shall We Start with a Foul?]
Dude, the angle on that spike was way too tight.

194
00:18:09,030 --> 00:18:11,908
Are you supposed to watch the blockers
before spiking?

195
00:18:11,908 --> 00:18:13,910
Don't you just time it and hit it?

196
00:18:15,953 --> 00:18:19,390
You're supposed to check the blockers
and choose between cross or line.

197
00:18:19,390 --> 00:18:21,542
But you have to decide right before you jump.

198
00:18:21,542 --> 00:18:23,419
If they read your setup, you'll get blocked.

199
00:18:24,337 --> 00:18:25,796
Hey, how do you know that?

200
00:18:26,496 --> 00:18:28,633
Because a setter has to calculate all that
before setting the ball.

201
00:18:29,560 --> 00:18:31,485
Depending on the toss direction and timing,

202
00:18:31,485 --> 00:18:33,596
the ace's attack angle completely changes.

203
00:18:34,388 --> 00:18:36,349
I guess that's how it is for a setter.

204
00:18:38,580 --> 00:18:40,661
That's why on the second spike today,

205
00:18:40,661 --> 00:18:42,271
